How to Set Up Third-Party Synthesis
You must synthesize DFT logic generated in the Tessent Shell flow in order to perform scan 
insertion, test pattern generation, and other processes. 
Solution
You must define constraints in synthesis tools to enable accurate gate level representations of 
the RTL. These constraints are primarily made up of clock definitions and timing constraints. 
Use the following procedures to set up constraints for Synopsys and Cadence synthesis tools 
within the Tessent Shell flow.
Synopsys
The following procedure provides a high-level overview of the synthesis flow for Synopsys. For 
complete details, refer to “Example Design Compiler Synthesis Script” on page 1019 for an 
example.
1. Source the SDC file generated by the tool.
The generated SDC file is located in the TSDB of the current design under the design ID 
to which the DFT was inserted and the ICL was extracted.

